{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>To all his people.</b> Since he saw that the midwives did not do as he had spoken to them, he made all his people appointees over them — this is 'Pharaoh charged all his people' — thinking that they would not be able to guard themselves against everyone. <b>Into the river you shall cast him.</b> Because Pharaoh's astrologers saw that a certain people was destined to be struck by water, and they thought to turn the decree upon Israel — therefore they said, 'into the river you shall cast him.'" "<b>And every daughter you shall let live.</b> They saw in their astrology that they were destined to drown only males, and so it was, for the men of war who pursued them drowned."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:43.491837887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}